      <div class="space-y-3 sm:space-y-4">
        <details class="group bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 p-4 sm:p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm md:text-base gap-2">
            <span>What is the core difference between SGPA and CGPA?</span>
            <span class="p-1 rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            <strong>SGPA (Semester Grade Point Average)</strong> reflects your performance in a single semester. <strong>CGPA (Cumulative Grade Point Average)</strong> is the cumulative weighted score of all your semesters combined across your entire degree.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 p-4 sm:p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm md:text-base gap-2">
            <span>Can I customize the calculator for my university's 5.0 or 10.0 scale?</span>
            <span class="p-1 rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Yes! Click the <strong>"Grade Scale"</strong> button at the top of the calculator. You can choose from presets like <strong>Standard 4.0</strong>, <strong>4.3 Scale</strong>, <strong>5.0 Scale (Nigerian/Intl)</strong>, or <strong>10.0 Scale (Indian UGC)</strong>, or manually edit each letter grade point value.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 p-4 sm:p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm md:text-base gap-2">
            <span>How do credit hours weight my courses?</span>
            <span class="p-1 rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Credit hours represent the academic weight of a class. A 4-credit calculus course impacts your GPA twice as much as a 2-credit elective course. The calculation multiplies credit hours by grade points to yield total Quality Points.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 p-4 sm:p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm md:text-base gap-2">
            <span>How do I convert my 10.0 CGPA to a percentage?</span>
            <span class="p-1 rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            In most Indian universities following UGC/AICTE guidelines, the formula is: <strong class="font-mono">Percentage (%) = CGPA × 9.5</strong>. For example, a CGPA of 8.4 converts to <span class="font-mono">8.4 × 9.5 = 79.8%</span>.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 p-4 sm:p-5 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm md:text-base gap-2">
            <span>Is this utility really 100% private?</span>
            <span class="p-1 rounded-lg bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Yes! All state management and mathematical calculations take place strictly within your browser's JavaScript engine. No course information, grades, or personal details are uploaded to any server.
          </p>
        </details>
